# Governance Assets

- Keep root `AGENTS.md` short and limited to stable invariants; every rule names the mechanism that enforces it or says `(prompt-only)` (`rules-audit`, `agents-lint`).
- A rule that names an enforcement point which does not exist is a phantom and fails the audit (`rules-audit`).
- Use focused `.mdc` rules with a valid `description`, `globs` when path-specific, and `alwaysApply`; keep always-applied rules few, because every request pays for them (prompt-only).
- Skills use kebab-case names equal to their folder, a description under 220 characters, and lowercase `disable-model-invocation` (`skills-lint`).
- Agent roles stay narrow; exploration, impact analysis, debugging, and review are `readonly: true` (prompt-only).
- Instruction files never redirect endpoints, embed credentials, override higher-authority instructions, or argue the agent out of its own verification (`instructions`).
- Use repository-relative POSIX paths and technology-neutral language; do not add executable skill scripts, only `node scripts/harness.mjs <command>` invocations (prompt-only).
